Ladybird clamps each border-image source slice to its corresponding
image dimension, and allows opposing slices to overlap. The corner
regions retain their full source extent, while empty edge and center
regions remain unpainted. Destination widths still shrink to fit the
border-image area without changing the source regions they sample.

Blink clamps source slices in ComputeEdgeSlice(), and constructs
its source regions from those values in NinePieceImageGrid. WebKit
clamps them independently in computeSlices(); paintNinePieceImage()
applies scaleSlicesIfNeeded() only to the destination slices. Gecko
clamps each mSlice in the nsCSSBorderImageRenderer constructor, and
applies overlap reduction to mWidths. Ladybird matches this source-
slice behavior in all three engines without changing its separate
destination-width reduction.
